  "nutritionSource": "USDA FoodData Central: Branded Foods labels (King Arthur Bread Flour, Morton) and SR Legacy (whole milk, active dry yeast, sugar, egg, butter, honey, powdered sugar). The honey butter is counted, split over 18 rolls. Water, cinnamon and the pan grease not counted.",
  "swaps": null,
  "notes": [
    "Why so soft: the cooked flour paste (tangzhong) holds extra water, so the rolls are fluffier and stay soft at least a day (Cook’s Illustrated). His version won a 42-taster dinner roll bake-off (The Pancake Princess).",
    "Changes from his recipe: doubled (his makes 9 in a 9×9 pan); folds instead of 5–7 min of mixer kneading; a honey-butter brush instead of plain butter and flaky salt. His charred-cinnamon honey butter is simplified (no vanilla bean, pepper or nutmeg; one honey).",
    "Eggs: the mediums on hand run ≈44 g, so weigh out 100 g for the dough. Instant yeast works the same way here."
  ],
